WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.050
Industrial threat hunting is the proactive,

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:06.785
defensive search for suspicious or unexplained activity in OT and ICS environments.

00:00:06.785 --> 00:00:08.795
Hunters do not wait for a confirmed alert.

00:00:08.795 --> 00:00:11.815
They begin with a focused question, examine available evidence,

00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:15.545
and determine whether the environment contains activity that existing monitoring missed or

00:00:15.545 --> 00:00:16.405
did not explain.

00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:18.665
Alert response starts with a generated signal.

00:00:18.665 --> 00:00:20.400
Hunting starts with a hypothesis,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.310
such as whether remote support reached an unexpected controller or whether engineering

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.500
activity occurred outside an approved window.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.170
A hunt may discover a security event, an operational fault, a policy gap,

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.750
or incomplete telemetry.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.590
OT hunting differs from ordinary enterprise hunting because technical evidence has

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.351
physical and operational meaning.

00:00:37.351 --> 00:00:42.130
A communication change may affect production, safety, reliability, or process integrity.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:46.005
The same behavior can be legitimate maintenance in one context and concerning in another.

00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:47.970
Hunts should be careful and evidence-driven.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.740
Use existing logs and passive telemetry where possible.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.520
Define scope, data sources, time range, owners, and stop conditions.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.485
Do not send unplanned probes, commands,

00:00:56.485 --> 00:01:00.305
or configuration changes to sensitive systems merely to create evidence.

00:01:00.305 --> 00:01:02.795
Operators and engineers are analytical partners.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:06.570
They explain process modes, maintenance, equipment behavior, and safe escalation.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.195
Security hunters contribute investigative structure and cross-source correlation.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:14.285
Together they can distinguish unexplained activity from known work or process failure.

00:01:14.285 --> 00:01:17.010
The goal is not disruption or proving a dramatic theory.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.280
It is better visibility, earlier detection, and safer decisions.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.700
A successful hunt can confirm the hypothesis, disprove it, identify a coverage gap,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.600
improve inventory, or produce a new detection that protects future operations.
